### `coordination_act`
Record canonical file ownership for already admitted work. Acquire uses the current registered checkout Git HEAD as sourceRevision. contentSha256 is the literal absent for a missing file, or SHA256 of exact current bytes for an existing file; SHA256(empty) denotes an existing empty file, not absence. This native observation port supports file claims only. Inspect original state before correcting a rejected request; unknown effects retain ownership and do not authorize replay. Claim inspection never grants permission to patch. Release or handoff requires an explicit reviewed effect disposition.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { coordination_act(args: { command: {
  action: "acquire";
  briefingSequence: number;
  claimId: string;
  claimRevision: number;
  // For a file that does not exist, use the literal string absent. For an existing file, use SHA256 of its exact current bytes (64 lowercase hex characters). An empty existing file has SHA256(empty); that digest must not represent a missing file. The native bridge independently observes the physical target before admission.
  contentSha256: string;
  // This native physical-observation port supports file claims only. Directory observation is not implemented.
  kind: "file";
  // Requested lease lifetime in whole seconds, from 1 through 3600 inclusive. Expiry does not release uncertain effects.
  leaseSeconds: number;
  note: string;
  relativePath: string;
  // Exact current Git HEAD revision (40 or 64 lowercase hex characters) of the registered physical checkout. Read it from that checkout; it is not a file digest or a prior claim revision.
  sourceRevision: string;
  workId: string;
  workRevision: number;
} | { action: "renew"; briefingSequence: number; claimId: string; claimRevision: number; leaseSeconds: number; note: string; workId: string; workRevision: number; } | { action: "release"; briefingSequence: number; claimId: string; claimRevision: number; effectDisposition: "reviewed" | "unknown"; note: string; workId: string; workRevision: number; } | { action: "handoff"; briefingSequence: number; claimId: string; claimRevision: number; effectDisposition: "reviewed" | "unknown"; note: string; targetWorkId: string; targetWorkRevision: number; workId: string; workRevision: number; } | { action: "accept"; briefingSequence: number; claimId: string; claimRevision: number; leaseSeconds: number; note: string; workId: string; workRevision: number; } | {
  action: "inspect";
  briefingSequence: number;
  claimId: string;
  // Wire-compatible hint only for inspection. Reads return the current claim; mutations require exact revision CAS.
  claimRevision: number;
  note: string;
  workId: string;
  workRevision: number;
}; }): Promise<unknown>; };
```

### `exec_command`
Runs a command in a PTY, returning output or a session ID for ongoing interaction.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { exec_command(args: {
  // Shell command to execute.
  cmd: string;
  // User-facing approval question for `require_escalated`; omit otherwise.
  justification?: string;
  // True runs the shell with -l/-i semantics; false disables them. Defaults to true.
  login?: boolean;
  // Output token budget. Defaults to 10000 tokens; larger requests may be capped by policy.
  max_output_tokens?: number;
  // Reusable approval prefix for `cmd`, only with `sandbox_permissions: "require_escalated"`; for example ["git", "pull"].
  prefix_rule?: Array<string>;
  // Per-command sandbox override. Defaults to `use_default`; use `require_escalated` for unsandboxed execution.
  sandbox_permissions?: "use_default" | "require_escalated";
  // Shell binary to launch. Defaults to the user's default shell.
  shell?: string;
  // True allocates a PTY for the command; false or omitted uses plain pipes.
  tty?: boolean;
  // Working directory for the command. Defaults to the turn cwd.
  workdir?: string;
  // Wait before yielding output. Defaults to 10000 ms; effective range is 250-30000 ms.
  yield_time_ms?: number;
}): Promise<{
  // Chunk identifier included when the response reports one.
  chunk_id?: string;
  // Process exit code when the command finished during this call.
  exit_code?: number;
  // Approximate token count before output truncation.
  original_token_count?: number;
  // Command output text, possibly truncated.
  output: string;
  // Session identifier to pass to write_stdin when the process is still running.
  session_id?: number;
  // Elapsed wall time spent waiting for output in seconds.
  wall_time_seconds: number;
}>; };
```

