### `hollywood_goal_adopt`
Accountable Goal manager: adopt the exact latest definition revision/digest after resolving its recorded questions. This records YOUR attributable review, never invents human approval. Read current Goal and any required real human answer first. Adoption fences older acceptance; existing unfinished effects require explicit reconciliation. No model/task starts.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { hollywood_goal_adopt(args: { definitionRevision: number; definitionSha256: string; goalId: string; note: string; revision: number; sourceEventId: string; }): Promise<unknown>; };
```

### `hollywood_goal_create`
Record a finite accountable Goal from this current accepted human/agent request or original native standing-role work. The canonical Role persists separately; Goal creation is not a chat self-request or a new human assignment. Optional roomId selects its collaboration room independently of agent context. For another room explicitly set publishScopedIntent=true: only selected Goal intent is published there, never private source text. Original source must be room-visible. reviewBudget bounds authorized material reviews; creation assigns no work. Native Goals require a developed/adopted definition and current strategy before Work assignment; use hollywood_goal_define/adopt/plan after reading the created Goal.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { hollywood_goal_create(args: { acceptance: string; objective: string; publishScopedIntent?: boolean; reviewBudget: number; roomId?: string | null; title: string; }): Promise<unknown>; };
```

### `hollywood_goal_define`
Develop or revise a Goal definition with concrete acceptance criteria and appropriate verification methods. Record assumptions and unresolved questions; discuss ambiguity with the relevant human through Hollywood. Artifact formats remain task-appropriate. Read current Goal first. definitionRevision is the latest proposed revision (0 initially). This proposes intent; it does not adopt, assign work or prove completion. sourceEventId must be readable room-visible Goal-local intent, such as the Goal source.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { hollywood_goal_define(args: { definition: { assumptions: Array<string>; criteria: Array<{ id: string; method: "command" | "artifact" | "review"; requirement: string; verification: string; }>; objective: string; openQuestions: Array<string>; }; definitionRevision: number; goalId: string; note: string; revision: number; sourceEventId: string; }): Promise<unknown>; };
```

### `hollywood_goal_plan`
Record a durable strategy against the adopted Goal definition: alternatives considered, selected approach and rationale, current frontier of existing Work IDs and conditions for replanning. One alternative is sufficient when warranted; do not invent ceremony. Existing Work owns dependencies and execution. Read current Goal/Work first. For changed adopted criteria, obsolete unfinished Work must be explicitly cancelled/settled; create replacement Work bound to current criteria before selecting it. Completed rejected Work has a separate revision path. Retain retired paths/effects; never relabel old evidence. This records no execution.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { hollywood_goal_plan(args: { definitionRevision: number; goalId: string; note: string; planRevision: number; revision: number; sourceEventId: string; strategy: { alternatives: Array<{ approach: string; id: string; tradeoffs: string; }>; frontierWorkIds: Array<string>; rationale: string; replanWhen: Array<string>; selected: string; }; }): Promise<unknown>; };
```

